{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794175237,"nonce":"WbnDGOK4tIue89Umba9E/xiw1zc=","message":"Landed on `roadmap-e90c710-integration` (740b08f..bda7576).\n\n**Changes**\n- src/epics.rs: new. `EpicSummary` and `summarize` (children matched per repo and ordered by layer; closed, total, in-progress and blocked counts; last activity as the newest edit by UTC instant; most recent first). Also `RepoCounts`, `count_open`, `epoch_secs`, `format_date`, with 11 unit tests.\n- src/lib.rs: exports `epics`.\n- src/gitbug/mod.rs: `current_user` (`git-bug user show --field name`) and `initials`, with a test.\n- src/app.rs: `epic_filter`, `epics`, `expanded`, `initials`. New messages `SetEpicStatus`, `PickEpicRepo`, `ToggleEpic`, `Identified`. `refilter` also refreshes the epic summaries. Identity is fetched once per discovery, from the first git-bug repo. 4 new tests.\n- src/ui/screen.rs: real Epics page with Open/Closed/All chips, a repo picker and cards that expand to list children. Overview page with per-repo cards. Avatar initials come from the git-bug identity, with `?` as fallback. The repo picker is now shared with the Issues filter bar.\n- src/mock.rs: deleted. The `mod mock` line in src/main.rs is removed and nothing references it.\n- docs/design.md: code map updated, mock notes removed.\n\n**Gates:** tests ok · clippy ok · fmt ok\n**Review:** 1 findings — 1 auto, 0 by hand, 0 deferred\n\n**Decisions**\n- Epics get their own `Filter` (status and repo only, default Open) so the Issues page filter is untouched. Epic filtering uses `filter::matches` on the epic itself. Children are always counted in full.\n- Children are matched on (repo, epic id) so clones that share git-bug ids never merge.\n- Last activity compares timestamps as UTC instants through a small RFC 3339 parser (no chrono dependency). Displayed dates use the timestamp's own offset.\n- Review fix: the Overview \"N open\" headline uses `RepoEntry::open_count()`, which counts every open issue including ones with no `kind:` label. The per-kind rows still count only epics, tasks and bugs, so they can sum to less than the headline.\n- The placeholder sections (Labels, Identities, Bridges, Analytics) keep the old placeholder header, since only Epics and Overview were in scope.\n- Commits on task-0ad0018: d97578b (feat), bda7576 (fix).","files":null}]}